#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:175
#, no-c-format
msgid "Generating the KParts &kde; 4 application"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:176
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A KParts component is a &kde; GUI component featuring a widget embeddedable "
"in any application and GUI elements that will be merged in the \"host\" user "
"interface (menubars, toolbars... ). It can embed in other &kde; "
"applications. For example, &konsole; is a KPart and can therefore be easily "
"used in KDevelop or &kate;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:178
#, no-c-format
msgid "The template will give you the following application:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:183
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>KParts application</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:189
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>KParts application</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:194
#, no-c-format
msgid "This template is a small editor"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:195
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can read more about KParts in this detailed tutorial: <ulink url="
"\"http://techbase.kde.org/Development/Architecture/KDE3/KParts\">http://"
"techbase.kde.org/Development/Architecture/KDE3/KParts</ulink>."
